t but you just got to  believe in the process you've got to  trust the process and not focus so much  on the results a lot of times when you  start out when you've got a side hustle  and you want to make it your full-time  thing or you want to be successful at it  it's tempting to look at the results and  to get discouraged because you don't see  the results coming fast enough but  what's more important to do is to figure  out what's the process that's going to  make this new business of this new  venture successful and then keep on  doing the process eventually the results  will come and ultimately all that you  have control over in life is the process  and executing executing is the most  important thing once you trust the  process the results will come but only  if you stay in the game long enough to  actually get those results way number  five is get help  it's really hard to do everything on  your own especially the parts of your  business that you're not really good at  or want to be good at and so I've been  looking at how can I enlist people to  help me in my business and what can I do  to give value back to them so as an  example when I was starting my business  when I started my Evan Carmichael  business  I've even made money from my first  company and selling it but I hate  spending money till I make you money and  so I started finding ways to partner up  with friends to get their input to get  their help my first website was built by  a friend of mine  for free he picked a logo in the font  and we've actually kept that pretty  consistent over all the years and I came  because a buddy of mine wanted to help  me out and so chances are there's a lot  of people in your network who will want  to help you out if you just ask not  everybody needs to be paid for the work  that they're doing and maybe you could  pay a little bit part time on the side  if your business is slowly growing and  getting up there if you can involve  other people on your mission in your